{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"gnarly-sinistrous-groundhog","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Operator remediation — apply the value_wo migration, scrub existing cleartext from remote state, and rotate the exposed crown-jewel secrets\n\nThis is the PROD-mutation follow-through for the code change landed under\n`finedrawn-closed-stud` (eb67-b96c-dcf0-4f86), which migrated every SSM SecureString\n**secret** parameter to terraform write-only arguments (`value_wo` / `value_wo_version`)\nso secret values are never persisted to terraform state (ADR 0105). The code change alone\ndoes NOT mutate prod; this ticket is the operator cutover.\n\n**Run this only AFTER the value_wo code change has landed on main.** Follow the procedure in\n`infra/runbooks/ssm-secret-write-only.md` §\"REMEDIATE the existing exposure\".\n\n### Steps\n1. `terraform apply` the value_wo migration. NOTE the one-time cutover reset: on this apply\n   `value_wo_version` goes absent -> 1 for each migrated slot, so the provider re-sends\n   `value_wo = \"CHANGEME\"` once and RESETS each live seeded secret to the placeholder. This is\n   intended (we rotate these secrets in the same window). `user_data.sh`'s CHANGEME fail-fast is\n   the safety net.\n2. In the SAME maintenance window, re-seed/ROTATE every affected secret out-of-band\n   (`aws ssm put-parameter --overwrite`). Rotate the crown-jewels explicitly — they were exposed\n   in cleartext in state and must be treated as compromised: Gerrit admin password, opcert\n   Ed25519 signing key, rebar-bot signing key, Anthropic API key, jira-api-token, SSH host keys.\n   Update every external system that trusts an old value (Gerrit account, Jira token, bot public\n   key, Anthropic console).\n3. VERIFY no SecureString value appears in state: `terraform state pull` must show `value: null`\n   (and no `value_wo`) for every migrated secret. Only the generated `opcert_origin_guard`\n   legitimately still resolves (via its random_password).\n4. SCRUB the historical cleartext from the state backend: the prior values persist in the retained\n   versions of `s3://rebar-tfstate-896586841071/rebar/prod/terraform.tfstate` (bucket versioning,\n   ~149 versions). Permanently delete the affected object versions (or roll the bucket / lifecycle-\n   expire old versions per data-handling policy). Rotated values are retired but still purge them.\n\n### Coordination\n- Coordinate with the SEPARATE \"rubied\" apply that is seeding 4 new MCP-PAT SSM params so the\n  state scrub covers those params too (they are also SecureString secrets under /rebar/prod/).\n- Cross-reference: ADR 0105 (docs/adr/0105-ssm-secrets-never-in-terraform-state.md) and the runbook\n  infra/runbooks/ssm-secret-write-only.md.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] value_wo migration applied to prod.\n- [ ] Every migrated secret re-seeded/rotated; crown-jewels rotated and external trust updated.\n- [ ] `terraform state pull` shows no SecureString secret value (all `value: null`, no `value_wo`).\n- [ ] Historical cleartext purged from the state bucket's retained versions.\n- [ ] rubied MCP-PAT params covered by the same scrub.","id":"097b-de23-bf12-4c38","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Operator: apply value_wo SSM migration, scrub cleartext from remote tfstate, rotate exposed crown-jewel secrets"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788026034664613001,"uuid":"c34a6d53-a482-4fe2-8eb7-2d719f984c6d"}